{"name":"Daydreaming","hex":"#f4f0e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"daydreaming","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of daydream"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of daydreaming; a daydream or reverie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daydreaming"}],"entries":[{"title":"Daydreaming","blocks":[{"text":"Daydreaming is a stream of consciousness that detaches from current external tasks when one's attention becomes focused on a more personal and internal direction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Daydreaming_Gentleman.jpg/330px-Daydreaming_Gentleman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daydreaming"},{"title":"Daydreaming (Radiohead song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Daydreaming\" is a song by the English rock band Radiohead, produced by Nigel Godrich. It was released as a download on 6 May 2016 as the second single from Radiohead's ninth studio album, A Moon Shaped Pool. The song is a piano ballad with strings arranged by the Radiohead guitarist Jonny Greenwood. The music video was directed by Paul Thomas Anderson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/Daydreaming_%28Radiohead%29_%28Front_Cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daydreaming_(Radiohead_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Helleu_-_Daydream.jpg/330px-Helleu_-_Daydream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Helleu_-_Daydream.jpg/330px-Helleu_-_Daydream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Daydream by Paul César Helleu","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHelleu_-_Daydream.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb